\section{Primordial Informational Field}

The Primordial Informational Field (PIF) is defined by an informational density 
$\rho_I(t,\mathbf{x})$ and flow velocity $\mathbf{v}_I(t,\mathbf{x})$.

The Informational Field Equation (IFE) is:
\begin{equation}
\partial_t \rho_I + \nabla \cdot (\rho_I \mathbf{v}_I)
= \alpha (\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v}_I) + \beta \rho_I^2,
\end{equation}
where $\alpha$ and $\beta$ are transport coefficients determined by the 
non-linear substrate dynamics.